---
// Accounting Equation Lab: markup only. Behavior lives in src/scripts/tools/accounting-equation.js
import '../../styles/tools/accounting-equation.css';
---
<div class="ae" data-tool="accounting-equation">
  <section class="ae-equation" aria-label="The accounting equation, current totals">
    <div class="ae-eq-term"><span class="k">Assets</span><span class="v" data-r="eq-a">$0</span></div>
    <span class="ae-eq-op" data-r="eq-sign" aria-label="equals">=</span>
    <div class="ae-eq-term"><span class="k">Liabilities</span><span class="v" data-r="eq-l">$0</span></div>
    <span class="ae-eq-op">+</span>
    <div class="ae-eq-term"><span class="k">Owner's Equity</span><span class="v" data-r="eq-e">$0</span></div>
  </section>

  <section class="ae-bench">
    <div class="ae-panel ae-card" data-r="card">
      <div class="ae-progress">
        <span data-r="progress">Transaction 1 of 12</span>
        <div class="ae-track" aria-hidden="true"><div class="ae-bar" data-r="bar"></div></div>
      </div>
      <p class="ae-text" data-r="text" aria-live="polite"></p>
      <p class="ae-prompt">Which accounts change, and by how much? Use a minus sign for a decrease.</p>
      <form class="ae-entry" data-r="entry" onsubmit="return false"></form>
      <p class="ae-preview" data-r="preview" role="status"></p>
      <p class="ae-feedback" data-r="feedback" role="status" hidden></p>
      <p class="ae-why" data-r="why" hidden></p>
      <div class="ae-actions">
        <button type="button" class="ae-btn primary" data-act="check">Check my entry</button>
        <button type="button" class="ae-btn" data-act="reveal">Show answer</button>
        <button type="button" class="ae-btn primary" data-act="next" hidden>Next transaction</button>
        <button type="button" class="ae-btn" data-act="restart" hidden>Start over</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ae-panel ae-sheet" aria-label="Balance sheet">
      <h2>Maya's Food Truck <span>Balance sheet</span></h2>
      <div class="ae-sheet-cols">
        <div>
          <h3>Assets</h3>
          <ul data-r="list-A"></ul>
          <p class="ae-total"><span>Total assets</span><span data-r="total-A">$0</span></p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Liabilities</h3>
          <ul data-r="list-L"></ul>
          <p class="ae-subtotal"><span>Total liabilities</span><span data-r="total-L">$0</span></p>
          <h3>Owner's Equity</h3>
          <ul data-r="list-E"></ul>
          <p class="ae-subtotal"><span>Total equity</span><span data-r="total-E">$0</span></p>
          <p class="ae-total"><span>Liabilities + Equity</span><span data-r="total-le">$0</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ae-lower">
    <div class="ae-panel">
      <h2>Journal</h2>
      <p class="ae-empty" data-r="journal-empty">Posted transactions show up here.</p>
      <div class="ae-table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Transaction</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody data-r="journal"></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ae-panel">
      <h2>Try it</h2>
      <ol class="ae-qs">
        <li>Transaction 3 traded $20,000 of cash for a truck. Did Maya get richer, poorer, or neither? How does the balance sheet prove it? <button type="button" class="ae-reveal">Hint</button><span class="ae-ans" hidden>Neither. Total assets did not change and equity did not move. One asset turned into another.</span></li>
        <li>Transactions 5 and 9 both brought in cash. Why did only one of them change owner's equity? <button type="button" class="ae-reveal">Hint</button><span class="ae-ans" hidden>Transaction 5 was new revenue. Transaction 9 collected money already earned in transaction 6, so it just turned receivables into cash.</span></li>
        <li>Can a transaction change only one account? Try to invent one, then explain what goes wrong. <button type="button" class="ae-reveal">Hint</button><span class="ae-ans" hidden>No. If one account changes and nothing else does, one side of the equation moves and the other doesn't. Every transaction touches at least two accounts.</span></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<script>
  import { initAccountingEquation } from '../../scripts/tools/accounting-equation.js';
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-tool="accounting-equation"]').forEach(initAccountingEquation);
</script>
